A||||6||FieroPerformance||New harmonic balancer different design? Please help.||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-02-2001||08:56 PM||||I just got my new harmonic balancer today and it isn’t identical to my old one. The number on the new one is 2616  L38S<P>I ordered it through the Chevy dealership. Is it just a new design or is it the wrong part?<P>When I line up the groves that slide over the crank key, non of the holes around the edge line up and the timing marks do not line up.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||11-02-2001||10:20 PM||||I would take it back. Sounds like the wrong one.||||reg||3
Z||000002||voyagerspe||11-02-2001||11:29 PM||||ive had the same problem.  lots of balancers have the marks in the wrong place.(probably because there 2 piece with that rubber "gasket" in there(i think there put together wrong))  The way I fix this. first find out where the mark is supposed to be. (#1 piston TDC) then cut a new grove with a dremal or some other cutting tool (hack saw) or you can simply paint a mark on your balance where the line is supposed to be.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-03-2001||12:37 PM||||It's the wrong balancer.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||11-03-2001||09:11 PM||||I have seen some for sale. They said you had to put new mark on them for timing as they did match the original mark position, other than that they were supposed to work. I still wouldn't trust them.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||David DeVoe||11-03-2001||11:25 PM||||Charlie,<BR>I have 2 complete 2.8 engines. One is out of a truck, not MPFI. The balancer and front cover from that engine are different than the ones from my Fiero engine. The timing mark on the balancer and the degree scale on the cover are in a different position. Sounds to me like you have one of those. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||11-04-2001||03:09 AM||||Hey Charlie!<BR>Your new "balancer" will work, if you remark the timing grove...<BR>I would suggest using a timing tape though...<BR>BTW, it really isn't a "balancer" but a dampener...<BR>The two piece design with a rubber core provides the dampening abillity...<BR>Also why it is a poor choice to time an engine from, as the outer ring can move...<BR>So where is the best place to time from? The flywheel...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
